"entity": {
"name": "Brunswick Corporation",
"description": "Brunswick Corp. engages in the design, manufacture, and marketing of recreational marine products, including marine engines, boats, and parts and accessories for those products. Brands include Mercury, Simrad, Lowrance, Boston Whaler, Sea Ray, Lund, Bayliner, and Freedom Boat Club. It operates through the following segments: Propulsion, Engine P&A, Boat, and Navico Group. The Propulsion segment manufactures outboard, sterndrive, and inboard engines and propulsion-related controls, propellers, and rigging parts and accessories. The Engine P&A segment supplies parts and accessories for marine and non-marine markets. The Boat segment designs and makes Sea Ray, Bayliner, Boston Whaler, Lund, Crestliner, Harris, Lowe, Princecraft and other boats. The Navico Group segment designs and markets electronics and systems for marine, RV, specialty vehicle, mobile, and industrial markets. The company was founded by John Moses Brunswick in 1845 and is headquartered in Mettawa, IL.",
